Spec: Android private stream socket SDK

Purpose:
  Turn an authorized Binder descriptor into a standard application-owned Java socket while retaining TLS semantics.

Owns:
  ./build.gradle
  ./src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
  ./README.md

Structure:
  ./src: Descriptor ownership, bounded socket adaptation and independent stream verification.

References:
  /android/client/client.sdd

Must:
  Depend only on the public client and framework; carry no Agent state, device keys, PKIX dependency or transport runtime.
  Declare INTERNET only for the private in-process socket adapter, without overriding application cleartext policy.
  Never return a public listening endpoint; verify the accepted socket against the held local client before forwarding any bytes.
  Preserve application HTTP authority, TLS checks and TCP half-close; close all owned descriptors after failure or cancellation.
